{"toolCallId":"call_8d2a952fe8ce45d98d01be2074e2d3ab","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"[What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.2 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n[2-3 sentence high-level overview for stakeholders who need quick context]\n\n**Key Decisions**: [Major decision 1], [Major decision 2]\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: [Blocking dependency]\n\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | [P0/P1/P2] |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n[What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\n\n### Purpose\n[One-sentence outcome statement. What does success look like?]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- [Deliverable 1]\n- [Deliverable 2]\n- [Deliverable 3]\n\n### Out of Scope\n- [Excluded item 1] - [why]\n- [Excluded item 2] - [why]\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| [path/to/file.js] | [Modify/Create/Delete] | [Brief description] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | [Requirement description] |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-002 | [Requirement description] |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: [Primary measurable outcome]\n- **SC-002**: [Secondary measurable outcome]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | [System/API] | [What if blocked] | [Fallback plan] |\n| Risk | [Risk description] | [High/Med/Low] | [Mitigation strategy] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: [Response time target - e.g., <200ms p95]\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: [Auth requirement - e.g., JWT tokens required]\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: [Uptime target - e.g., 99.9%]\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: [How system handles]\n- Maximum length: [Limit and behavior]\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- External service failure: [Fallback behavior]\n- Network timeout: [Retry strategy]\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | [/25] | [Files: X, LOC: Y, Systems: Z] |\n| Risk | [/25] | [Auth: Y/N, API: Y/N, Breaking: Y/N] |\n| Research | [/20] | [Investigation needs] |\n| Multi-Agent | [/15] | [Workstreams: X] |\n| Coordination | [/15] | [Dependencies: X] |\n| **Total** | **[/100]** | **Level 3** |\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | [Risk] | [H/M/L] | [H/M/L] | [Strategy] |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: [Title] (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** [user type], **I want** [needed behavior], **so that** [benefit].\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: [Title] (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** [user type], **I want** [needed behavior], **so that** [benefit].\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- [Question 1 requiring clarification]\n- [Question 2 requiring clarification]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `decision-record.md`\n\n---\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"recommend-level.sh always prints its full scored report, so a caller that needs only the level has to parse the block. A --quiet flag prints that one line and nothing else.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\n  - \"quiet level recommendation output\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.2 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n`recommend-level.sh` is the deterministic level scorer every SpecKit packet starts from, and it always writes a human report of five to fifteen lines. Any caller that wants the single recommended level has to parse that report, which couples the caller to the report's layout. `--quiet` makes the one value the script exists to produce available on its own, without changing what the script prints for anyone who does not pass the flag.\n\n**Key Decisions**: `--quiet` is text-mode only and `--json` takes precedence over it, so no machine-readable consumer sees a different document; the suppressed output is the whole human report rather than only its breakdown, so the flag really does leave one line.\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: none outside the script. Bash 3.2 compatibility is the only environmental constraint, and the file already targets it.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `HEAD` (detached; the packet was scaffolded with `--skip-branch`) |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\nrecommend-level.sh always prints its full scored report, so a caller that needs only the level has to parse the block. The report is a blank line, the `Recommended Level: N (Name)` line, a score and confidence line, a four-row point breakdown and, unless phase output is disabled, a phase-recommendation block. A shell pipeline that picks a template set, or an agent recording one value, therefore reaches for `grep '^Recommended Level:'` or `sed`, and any future edit to the report silently breaks that parse. There is no supported way to ask the script for the single line it exists to produce.\n\n### Purpose\nAdd a `--quiet` flag that prints only the final recommended-level line, while every existing invocation keeps its current output byte for byte.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Accept `--quiet` as a valueless flag in the existing argument-parsing loop, in any position among the other flags.\n- Suppress the whole human report in quiet mode and print exactly one line: `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)`.\n- Leave text output, JSON output, help output, error output and exit codes unchanged for every invocation that does not pass `--quiet`.\n- Document the flag where the script already documents its flags: the header comment block, the `--help` text and the examples.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- `--json` output shape and content - a JSON document is already a single machine-readable artifact, and changing it would break consumers that parse it today.\n- Any other script in `runtime/cli/spec/` - `create.sh`, `upgrade-level.sh` and `validate.sh` have their own output contracts and none of them needs this flag.\n- A short form such as `-q` - the script uses `-j` and `-h` only, and adding a letter alias is a separate compatibility decision.\n- Suppressing stderr diagnostics - errors stay on stderr with their current text and exit code 1.\n- Rewriting the scoring algorithm, thresholds or phase logic - the change touches argument parsing and output selection only.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Modify | Add the `QUIET_OUTPUT` global, the `--quiet` parse arm, a quiet branch at the top of `output_text()`, and the flag's entries in the header comment and `--help` text. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--quiet` is accepted as a valueless flag by the argument-parsing loop, in any argument position, and repeated occurrences are idempotent. |\n| REQ-002 | With `--quiet` and text output, stdout holds exactly one line, `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)`, with no leading blank line, no score line, no breakdown and no phase block. |\n| REQ-003 | Every invocation that does not pass `--quiet` produces output identical to the pre-change script, including the leading and trailing blank lines, the phase block and the `--no-recommend-phases` variant. |\n| REQ-004 | Exit codes are unchanged: `0` on success, `1` for a missing flag value, a non-numeric value, both inputs zero and an unknown option. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-005 | `--json` takes precedence over `--quiet`: passing both prints the unchanged JSON document, and the flag is documented as text-mode only. |\n| REQ-006 | `--help` lists `--quiet` with its one-line description, and the script's header comment block lists it beside the other options. |\n| REQ-007 | `--quiet` composes with `--no-recommend-phases`, `--phase-threshold`, `--auth`, `--api`, `--db` and `--architectural` without altering their scoring. |\n| REQ-008 | The flag is implemented with constructs the file already uses, so the script still runs under the Bash 3.2 that ships with macOS. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet` writes exactly one stdout line, `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)`, and exits `0`.\n- **SC-002**: A golden-output capture of the twelve-invocation matrix in `tasks.md` is byte-identical before and after the change for every invocation that omits `--quiet`.\n- **SC-003**: `--help` mentions `--quiet`, and `--quiet --help` still prints the full help text.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | Bash 3.2 on macOS | A construct the newer shell allows would fail on the developer's own machine | Use only the `case`, `[[ ]]` and `echo` forms already present in the file; run the script under the system bash. |\n| Dependency | The existing text report's exact bytes | A stray edit in `output_text()` changes output for every caller | Capture the golden matrix before the edit and diff after it; the diff is the acceptance proof. |\n| Risk | Quiet mode drifts from the report's wording | The line a caller parses stops matching the line the full report prints | Derive the quiet line from the same `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL` and `LEVEL_NAME` globals and the same format string; compare both outputs in one task. |\n| Risk | A caller passes `--quiet --json` and expects a level line | It receives JSON instead, which is not what the flag's name suggests | Document the precedence in `--help` and in this spec, and assert the JSON-unchanged behaviour in the verification matrix. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: The flag adds no measurable work. The quiet path prints one line where the full path prints at least five, and the script stays far below 100 ms wall time for any input, which is the only budget this CLI has.\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: The flag introduces no input surface. It is a boolean with no value, so it adds no parsing, no path handling and no environment read, and the script continues to read nothing but its own arguments.\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: Output is deterministic. The same arguments produce the same bytes on every run, in both modes, because the change introduces no clock, locale or filesystem dependency.\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: `--quiet` with neither `--loc` nor `--files` keeps the existing `ERROR: At least --loc or --files must be provided` path, exit `1`, and prints no level line.\n- Maximum length: no new bound. The quiet line's length depends only on the level digit and the level name, both of which come from a fixed four-value set.\n- Repeated flag: `--quiet --quiet` behaves as one occurrence, because the parse arm sets a boolean rather than incrementing anything.\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- External service failure: not applicable. The script has no network, database or filesystem dependency.\n- Network timeout: not applicable, for the same reason.\n- Invalid flag value: `--quiet` takes no value, so `--quiet 5` leaves `5` to be rejected by the catch-all arm as `ERROR: Unknown option: 5`, exit `1`, exactly as an unmatched positional argument is rejected today.\n- Combined with `--json`: JSON wins and the document is unchanged; the quiet branch lives in `output_text()` and is never reached from the JSON path.\n- Combined with `--help`: help exits `0` inside the parse loop before any output mode is chosen, so `--quiet --help` prints the full help text.\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | 6/25 | Files: 1, LOC: ~20 net, Systems: 1 |\n| Risk | 3/25 | Auth: N, API: N, Breaking: N (opt-in flag only) |\n| Research | 3/20 | The script, its help text and its callers were read; no external investigation needed |\n| Multi-Agent | 1/15 | Workstreams: 1 |\n| Coordination | 2/15 | Dependencies: 0 |\n| **Total** | **15/100** | **Level 3 (declared by the scaffold instruction; the scoring model would return Level 0)** |\n\nThe declared level and the score disagree on purpose. This packet was scaffolded with `--level 3` by the dispatch instruction, not chosen from the score above. The extra structure is documentation depth: the work itself is a single-file, opt-in flag, and a reader should not infer a large change from the level marker.\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | A refactor of `output_text()` changes the default report while adding the branch | H | L | Golden-output diff over the twelve-invocation matrix before and after the edit. |\n| R-002 | Quiet line wording diverges from the report's wording | M | L | Both paths print the same format string from the same globals. |\n| R-003 | A shell construct breaks under Bash 3.2 | M | L | Copy the existing `case` and `[[ ]]` idioms; run under `/bin/bash`. |\n| R-004 | A caller expects `--quiet --json` to yield the level line | L | M | Precedence stated in `--help`, in REQ-005 and in ADR-001, and asserted in the matrix. |\n| R-005 | A future flag addition reuses the name | L | L | The name is documented in the header block beside every other option. |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: One-line level for a scripted caller (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** shell script or agent choosing a documentation level, **I want** `recommend-level.sh --quiet` to print only the recommended-level line, **so that** I can read the level without a `grep` or `sed` expression that breaks when the report changes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: Unchanged report for an interactive reader (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** developer running the script by hand, **I want** the existing report to look exactly as it does today, **so that** I lose no score, breakdown or phase information and my notes and examples stay valid.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- None blocking. The one ambiguity this feature carries - what `--quiet` means when `--json` is also passed - is decided in REQ-005 and recorded as ADR-001 in `plan.md`; reopen it only if a consumer asks for a quiet JSON variant.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See the L3 Architecture Decision Record in `plan.md`\n\n---\n\n\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":65,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":41}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_8e8e15b1d5fd46688c413d11bdfd0bdf","title":"Read lines 255-360 in ./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/graph/generated-metadata-drift.ts","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"sed -n '255,360p' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/graph/generated-metadata-drift.ts","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"sed -n '255,360p' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/graph/generated-metadata-drift.ts"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/commandNames":["sed"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_95e636c55b3e457b8c474f4c7fe9cc46","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### Description (file path). Twelve ordered tasks: read the anchors, capture the twelve-row baseline, add the global, the parse arm and the quiet guard, document the flag in two places, then prove the default report is byte-identical and the quiet row is one line.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\n  - \"quiet flag implementation tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`\n\n**Path convention.** Run every command from the repository root. `SCRIPT` means `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` and `PACKET` means `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag`. A path written as `scratch/<name>` means `$PACKET/scratch/<name>`. The shell does not expand `$SCRIPT` or `$PACKET` unless a task sets them, so every command block below sets them itself.\n\n**Anchor convention.** Every line number in this document was read on the scaffold commit. `recommend-level.sh` is edited by this packet alone, so the numbers hold until T003 inserts a line; T004 and later quote the anchor text instead of relying on the number. Locate the quoted text and edit there. Never delete a range you have not read.\n\n**Insertion order.** T003 inserts into the globals block, above every anchor T004 and T005 touch. T004 inserts a `case` arm above `--json|-j`. T005 inserts at the top of `output_text()`'s body. Working top-down keeps each later anchor's line number valid.\n\n**Comment hygiene.** No task adds a packet number, an AC-id, an R-id or a task id to a comment in the script. The script's comments state what the code does; the spec documents carry the identifiers.\n\n**Scope guard.** The only file this packet writes outside `$PACKET` is `$SCRIPT`. Every other path is read-only.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the four anchors and record their line numbers (`scratch/anchors.md`)\n\nFile: `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/anchors.md` (new file). Anchor: none.\n\nChange: read `$SCRIPT` and record one row per anchor below - the anchor text, its line number, and the enclosing function - so a later task that finds a moved line can tell a shift from a different edit.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nPACKET=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\ngrep -n '^JSON_OUTPUT=false$' \"$SCRIPT\"\ngrep -n '^    --json|-j)$' \"$SCRIPT\"\ngrep -n '^output_text() {$' \"$SCRIPT\"\ngrep -n '^show_help() {$' \"$SCRIPT\"\ngrep -c '^#   --' \"$SCRIPT\"\n```\n\nExpected: the four anchors print at lines `122`, `706`, `508` and `162`; the option count is `11`. Record the numbers as printed, whatever they are.\n\nRollback: `rm -f \"$PACKET/scratch/anchors.md\"`.\n\nStop and escalate if: any of the four anchors is absent, or the option count is not `11`.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T002 [P] Capture the twelve-row baseline matrix (`scratch/golden/`)\n\nFile: `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/golden/` (new directory). Anchor: none.\n\nChange: run each row below against the unmodified script and write three files per row: `M<row>.out` (stdout), `M<row>.err` (stderr) and `M<row>.code` (exit status). This capture is the only proof that the default report is unchanged, so it must be taken before T003.\n\n| Row | Arguments | Expected level |\n|-----|-----------|----------------|\n| M01 | `--loc 50 --files 2` | 0 (Quick) |\n| M02 | `--loc 200 --files 5 --api` | 1 (Baseline) |\n| M03 | `--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural` | 3 (Full) |\n| M04 | `--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --recommend-phases` | 3 (Full) |\n| M05 | `--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --no-recommend-phases` | 3 (Full) |\n| M06 | `--loc 100 --files 3 --json` | 0 (Quick) |\n| M07 | `--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --json --no-recommend-phases` | 3 (Full) |\n| M08 | `--help` | help text |\n| M09 | `--loc` | exit 1, `--loc requires a numeric value` |\n| M10 | `--loc 0 --files 0` | exit 1, `At least --loc or --files must be provided` |\n| M11 | `--bogus` | exit 1, `Unknown option: --bogus` |\n| M12 | `--phase-threshold 30 --loc 900 --files 20 --architectural --auth --api` | 3 (Full) |\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nPACKET=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\nmkdir -p \"$PACKET/scratch/golden\"\ni=0\nwhile IFS= read -r args; do\n  i=$((i + 1))\n  row=$(printf 'M%02d' \"$i\")\n  bash \"$SCRIPT\" $args > \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/$row.out\" 2> \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/$row.err\"\n  echo $? > \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/$row.code\"\ndone <<'ROWS'\n--loc 50 --files 2\n--loc 200 --files 5 --api\n--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural\n--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --recommend-phases\n--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --no-recommend-phases\n--loc 100 --files 3 --json\n--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --json --no-recommend-phases\n--help\n--loc\n--loc 0 --files 0\n--bogus\n--phase-threshold 30 --loc 900 --files 20 --architectural --auth --api\nROWS\nls \"$PACKET/scratch/golden\" | wc -l\ncat \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/M01.out\" | head -2\ncat \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/M09.code\" \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/M10.code\" \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/M11.code\"\n```\n\nExpected: `36` files; M01's second line is `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)`; each of the three `.code` files reads `1`, printed as three separate lines. If the loop stops early because `set -e` is active in the calling shell, run it with `set +e` first - the three error rows are expected to exit `1` and must still be recorded.\n\nRollback: `rm -r \"$PACKET/scratch/golden\"`.\n\nStop and escalate if: any row's level differs from the table, or a `.code` file is empty.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T003 Add the `QUIET_OUTPUT` global (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n\nFile: `$SCRIPT`. Anchor: the line `JSON_OUTPUT=false`, which T001 recorded at line 122.\n\nChange: add `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` on the line directly below `JSON_OUTPUT=false`, inside the same output-mode group and above the phase-recommendation flags. No comment line is added; the neighbouring globals carry none either.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\ngrep -n -A1 '^JSON_OUTPUT=false$' \"$SCRIPT\"\nbash -n \"$SCRIPT\" && echo SYNTAX_OK\n```\n\nExpected: `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` is the next line after `JSON_OUTPUT=false`; `SYNTAX_OK`.\n\nRollback: delete the `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` line.\n\nStop and escalate if: `JSON_OUTPUT=false` is not unique in the file, or `bash -n` fails.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T004 Add the `--quiet` parse arm (`$SCRIPT`)\n\nFile: `$SCRIPT`. Anchor: the text `    --json|-j)`, which T001 recorded at line 706.\n\nChange: insert one arm directly above the `--json|-j` arm:\n\n```bash\n    --quiet)\n      QUIET_OUTPUT=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n```\n\nThe arm takes no value, so it has no numeric guard. It sits above `--json|-j` rather than below it so the two output-mode switches stay adjacent and the `--json|-j` anchor does not move for T005.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\ngrep -n -B1 -A3 '^    --quiet)$' \"$SCRIPT\"\nbash -n \"$SCRIPT\" && echo SYNTAX_OK\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet | cat -A | head -3\n```\n\nExpected: the arm prints with its three body lines; `SYNTAX_OK`; the run prints the full report unchanged, because T005 has not added the guard yet - that is the expected intermediate state, and it confirms the flag parses without altering behaviour.\n\nRollback: delete the four inserted lines.\n\nStop and escalate if: `bash -n` fails, or the run reports `Unknown option: --quiet`.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T005 Add the quiet guard to `output_text()` (`$SCRIPT`)\n\nFile: `$SCRIPT`. Anchor: the text `output_text() {`, which T001 recorded at line 508, and the `echo \"\"` that follows it.\n\nChange: make the guard the first statement of the function body, above the leading `echo \"\"`:\n\n```bash\n  if [[ \"$QUIET_OUTPUT\" = true ]]; then\n    echo \"Recommended Level: ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL} (${LEVEL_NAME})\"\n    return 0\n  fi\n```\n\nThe format string is copied from the report's own level line rather than rewritten, so the two cannot drift. `output_json()` is not touched.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\ngrep -n -A5 '^output_text() {$' \"$SCRIPT\"\nbash -n \"$SCRIPT\" && echo SYNTAX_OK\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet | wc -l\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet\n```\n\nExpected: the guard is the first statement; `SYNTAX_OK`; the line count is `1`; the line reads `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)`.\n\nRollback: delete the four inserted lines.\n\nStop and escalate if: the line count is not `1`, the line text differs, or the guard landed outside `output_text()`.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T006 Document the flag in the header comment block (`$SCRIPT`)\n\nFile: `$SCRIPT`. Anchor: the header lines `#   --json, -j           Output in JSON format` and `#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --json`.\n\nChange: add one `OPTIONS` line below the `--json, -j` line, in the same column layout:\n\n```\n#   --quiet              Print only the recommended-level line (text output)\n```\n\nand one example below the existing JSON example:\n\n```\n#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --quiet\n```\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\ngrep -c '^#   --quiet ' \"$SCRIPT\"\ngrep -c '^#   Recommend-level.sh .*--quiet$' \"$SCRIPT\"\n```\n\nExpected: `1` and `1`.\n\nRollback: delete the two inserted comment lines.\n\nStop and escalate if: either count is `0` after the edit, or the inserted line breaks the column alignment of the neighbouring options.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T007 Document the flag in `show_help()` (`$SCRIPT`)\n\nFile: `$SCRIPT`. Anchor: the help lines `  --json, -j           Output in JSON format` and `  recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --json`.\n\nChange: add one `OPTIONS` row below the `--json, -j` row, in the same two-column layout:\n\n```\n  --quiet              Print only the recommended-level line (text output)\n```\n\nand one example below the JSON example:\n\n```\n  # Quiet output for scripting\n  recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --quiet\n```\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --help | grep -c -- '--quiet'\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --help | grep -c 'SpecKit Level Recommendation Algorithm'\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --help > /dev/null; echo $?\n```\n\nExpected: `2` for the first command, one `OPTIONS` row and one example; `1` for the second, proving `--quiet --help` still prints the full help; `0` for the exit status.\n\nRollback: delete the three inserted help lines.\n\nStop and escalate if: the help text no longer matches the header block's wording, or `--help` exits non-zero.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T008 Static checks and a first smoke run (`$SCRIPT`)\n\nFile: `$SCRIPT`. Anchor: none.\n\nChange: no edit. Run the syntax check, confirm the interpreter, and run the two headline invocations before starting the matrix.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nbash -n \"$SCRIPT\" && echo SYNTAX_OK\n/bin/bash --version | head -1\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 50 --files 2 | sed -n '2p'\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet\ncommand -v shellcheck >/dev/null && shellcheck -S warning \"$SCRIPT\" && echo SHELLCHECK_OK || echo SHELLCHECK_UNAVAILABLE\n```\n\nExpected: `SYNTAX_OK`; a `GNU bash, version 3.2` or newer line; `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)` from the report's second line; the same text as the only quiet line; `SHELLCHECK_OK` or `SHELLCHECK_UNAVAILABLE`.\n\nRollback: none - this task writes nothing.\n\nStop and escalate if: `bash -n` fails, or the two level lines differ.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T009 Prove the default report is unchanged across the twelve-row matrix\n\nFile: `scratch/verify/M*.out` (new directory). Anchor: none.\n\nChange: no edit. Rerun every row from T002 against the modified script into `scratch/verify/` and diff each pair.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nPACKET=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\nmkdir -p \"$PACKET/scratch/verify\"\ni=0\nwhile IFS= read -r args; do\n  i=$((i + 1))\n  row=$(printf 'M%02d' \"$i\")\n  bash \"$SCRIPT\" $args > \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/$row.out\" 2> \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/$row.err\"\n  echo $? > \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/$row.code\"\ndone <<'ROWS'\n--loc 50 --files 2\n--loc 200 --files 5 --api\n--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural\n--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --recommend-phases\n--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --no-recommend-phases\n--loc 100 --files 3 --json\n--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --json --no-recommend-phases\n--help\n--loc\n--loc 0 --files 0\n--bogus\n--phase-threshold 30 --loc 900 --files 20 --architectural --auth --api\nROWS\ndiff -r \"$PACKET/scratch/golden\" \"$PACKET/scratch/verify\" && echo GOLDEN_IDENTICAL\n```\n\nExpected: `GOLDEN_IDENTICAL`, and `diff` exits `0`. Any printed difference is a failure, not a tolerance.\n\nRollback: `rm -r \"$PACKET/scratch/verify\"`.\n\nStop and escalate if: `diff` reports a difference. Restore the script with `git checkout -- \"$SCRIPT\"` and record which row drifted before retrying.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T010 Verify the quiet contract on every quiet row\n\nFile: `scratch/verify/quiet.txt` (new file). Anchor: none.\n\nChange: no edit. Run the eight quiet rows, write their stdout and exit codes, and confirm each produces exactly one line with the expected text.\n\n| Row | Arguments | Expected stdout | Exit |\n|-----|-----------|-----------------|------|\n| Q01 | `--quiet --loc 50 --files 2` | `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)` | 0 |\n| Q02 | `--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet` | `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)` | 0 |\n| Q03 | `--quiet --quiet --loc 200 --files 5 --api` | `Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)` | 0 |\n| Q04 | `--json --quiet --loc 100 --files 3` | the unchanged JSON document from M06 | 0 |\n| Q05 | `--quiet --no-recommend-phases --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural` | `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)` | 0 |\n| Q06 | `--quiet --help` | the full help text from M08 | 0 |\n| Q07 | `--quiet --loc` | empty stdout; stderr names the missing value | 1 |\n| Q08 | `--quiet` | empty stdout; stderr asks for `--loc` or `--files` | 1 |\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nPACKET=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n{\n  bash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --loc 50 --files 2\n  bash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet\n  bash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --quiet --loc 200 --files 5 --api\n  bash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --no-recommend-phases --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural\n} > \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/quiet.txt\"\nwc -l < \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/quiet.txt\"\ncat \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/quiet.txt\"\nhead -c 1 \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/quiet.txt\"; echo\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --json --quiet --loc 100 --files 3 | diff - \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/M06.out\" && echo JSON_UNCHANGED\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --help | diff - \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/M08.out\" && echo HELP_UNCHANGED\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --loc > /dev/null 2> \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/Q07.err\"; echo \"Q07=$?\"\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet > /dev/null 2> \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/Q08.err\"; echo \"Q08=$?\"\ncat \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/Q07.err\" \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/Q08.err\"\n```\n\nExpected: `4` lines; the four lines read `0 (Quick)`, `3 (Full)`, `1 (Baseline)`, `3 (Full)` in that order; `head -c 1` prints `R`, proving there is no leading blank line; `JSON_UNCHANGED`; `HELP_UNCHANGED`; `Q07=1`; `Q08=1`; the two stderr files carry the existing messages.\n\nRollback: `rm -f \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/quiet.txt\" \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/Q07.err\" \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/Q08.err\"`.\n\nStop and escalate if: any quiet row prints more than one line, a level differs from the table, or either precedence diff reports a change.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T011 Verify the flag's placement independence and the rejection path\n\nFile: none. Anchor: none.\n\nChange: no edit. Prove that argument position does not matter and that `--quiet` takes no value.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\na=$(bash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --loc 200 --files 5 --api)\nb=$(bash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --quiet)\nc=$(bash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc --quiet 200 --files 5 --api 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\")\nprintf '%s\\n%s\\n%s\\n' \"$a\" \"$b\" \"$c\"\n[ \"$a\" = \"$b\" ] && echo POSITION_INDEPENDENT\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet 5 --loc 50 --files 2 > /dev/null 2>&1; echo \"VALUE_REJECTED=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: `a` and `b` are both `Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)`; `POSITION_INDEPENDENT`; `c` shows the existing numeric-value error and `exit=1`; `VALUE_REJECTED=1`.\n\nRollback: none - this task writes nothing.\n\nStop and escalate if: `a` and `b` differ, or the value-rejection path returns `0`.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T012 Record the evidence and clean the scratch directory\n\nFile: `tasks.md` (this document) and `scratch/`. Anchor: none.\n\nChange: no code edit. Update the Verification Summary's `Verified` column for each item as its proof lands, mark every completed item `[x]` with its command and observed result, and remove the working files the packet does not need to keep. The two golden directories are evidence, so keep `scratch/golden/` and `scratch/verify/` until the packet closes; delete `scratch/anchors.md` once the anchors are no longer needed.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nPACKET=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/check-completion.sh \"$PACKET\" || true\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$PACKET\" --strict | tail -3\n```\n\nExpected: `check-completion.sh` reports the checklist state without a P0 or P1 item marked complete and unevidenced; `validate.sh` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n\nRollback: none - the evidence is additive.\n\nStop and escalate if: a completed P0 or P1 item has no evidence line, or `validate.sh` prints a failure.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] Code passes lint/format checks\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No console errors or warnings\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling implemented\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] Code follows project patterns\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Manual testing complete\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed, or instance-only status proven by grep.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for changed helpers, policies, schema fields, response fields, docs, and tests.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Security/path/parser/redaction fixes include adversarial table tests for delimiter, joined-input, outside-root, no-op, and fallback cases.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile env/global-state variant executed when tests or code read process-wide state.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a fix SHA or explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation implemented\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] Auth/authz working correctly\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Code comments adequate\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README updated (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files in scratch/ only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] scratch/ cleaned before completion\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 15 | 0/15 |\n| P1 Items | 23 | 0/23 |\n| P2 Items | 9 | 0/9 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-26\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\nThe packet's one architecture decision, ADR-001, is recorded in the L3 Architecture Decision Record section of `plan.md`; this packet has no separate `decision-record.md`, so CHK-100 and CHK-101 read against that section.\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] Architecture decisions documented in decision-record.md\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] All ADRs have status (Proposed/Accepted)\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path documented (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] Response time targets met (NFR-P01)\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] Throughput targets met (NFR-P02)\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] Load testing completed\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] Performance benchmarks documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented and tested\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] Feature flag configured (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] Monitoring/alerting configured\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] Runbook created\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Deployment runbook reviewed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review completed\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses compatible\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP Top 10 checklist completed\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling compliant with requirements\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation complete (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| Packet author | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| Operator | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| Packet author | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n---\n\n## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n- [ ] Read this document and confirm the task id, its file, its quoted anchor and its line number.\n- [ ] Re-read the file the task edits; confirm the quoted anchor still sits where T001 recorded it and belongs to the function the task names.\n- [ ] Confirm the task is not `[B]`; if it is, record the blocker and stop before editing.\n- [ ] Confirm T002's golden capture exists and is non-empty before any edit to `$SCRIPT`. Without it, the unchanged-output claim cannot be proven.\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Run T001 to T012 in order. T002 is `[P]` only against T001, because the capture must exist before T003 edits the script. |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Write only `$SCRIPT` and `$PACKET/scratch/`. Every other path is read-only. |\n| TASK-PROOF | Run the task's check and read both its output and its exit status before marking the task `[x]`. |\n| TASK-ANCHOR | Locate the quoted text. A moved line is not a changed edit; an absent anchor is a stop, not a nearby edit. |\n| TASK-COMMENT | No comment, help row or example added by this packet carries a task id, an AC-id or a packet number. |\n| TASK-OUTPUT | Never \"fix\" a golden-diff difference by recapturing the baseline. The baseline is the pre-change contract; a difference means the edit is wrong. |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\nAfter each task: `Task T### complete. Files: <paths>. Proof: <command> -> <observed output/exit>.` At a phase boundary, report the task range, the files changed and the gate that passed.\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\nIf a task cannot run, stop and record the blocker in `scratch/blocked.md` with the task id, the command that failed and its output. Do not substitute a different file, a different value or a different command. A `[B]` task stays blocked until its dependency's proof exists; a failed gate is repaired, not waived.\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### Description (file path). Twelve ordered tasks: read the anchors, capture the twelve-row baseline, add the global, the parse arm and the quiet guard, document the flag in two places, then prove the default report is byte-identical and the quiet row is one line.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\n  - \"quiet flag implementation tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`\n\n**Path convention.** Run every command from the repository root. `SCRIPT` means `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` and `PACKET` means `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag`. A path written as `scratch/<name>` means `$PACKET/scratch/<name>`. The shell does not expand `$SCRIPT` or `$PACKET` unless a task sets them, so every command block below sets them itself.\n\n**Anchor convention.** Every line number in this document was read on the scaffold commit. `recommend-level.sh` is edited by this packet alone, so the numbers hold until T003 inserts a line; T004 and later quote the anchor text instead of relying on the number. Locate the quoted text and edit there. Never delete a range you have not read.\n\n**Insertion order.** T003 inserts into the globals block, above every anchor T004 and T005 touch. T004 inserts a `case` arm above `--json|-j`. T005 inserts at the top of `output_text()`'s body. Working top-down keeps each later anchor's line number valid.\n\n**Comment hygiene.** No task adds a packet number, an AC-id, an R-id or a task id to a comment in the script. The script's comments state what the code does; the spec documents carry the identifiers.\n\n**Scope guard.** The only file this packet writes outside `$PACKET` is `$SCRIPT`. Every other path is read-only.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the four anchors and record their line numbers (`scratch/anchors.md`)\n\nFile: `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/anchors.md` (new file). Anchor: none.\n\nChange: read `$SCRIPT` and record one row per anchor below - the anchor text, its line number, and the enclosing function - so a later task that finds a moved line can tell a shift from a different edit.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nPACKET=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\ngrep -n '^JSON_OUTPUT=false$' \"$SCRIPT\"\ngrep -n '^    --json|-j)$' \"$SCRIPT\"\ngrep -n '^output_text() {$' \"$SCRIPT\"\ngrep -n '^show_help() {$' \"$SCRIPT\"\ngrep -c '^#   --' \"$SCRIPT\"\n```\n\nExpected: the four anchors print at lines `122`, `706`, `508` and `162`; the option count is `11`. Record the numbers as printed, whatever they are.\n\nRollback: `rm -f \"$PACKET/scratch/anchors.md\"`.\n\nStop and escalate if: any of the four anchors is absent, or the option count is not `11`.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T002 [P] Capture the twelve-row baseline matrix (`scratch/golden/`)\n\nFile: `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/golden/` (new directory). Anchor: none.\n\nChange: run each row below against the unmodified script and write three files per row: `M<row>.out` (stdout), `M<row>.err` (stderr) and `M<row>.code` (exit status). This capture is the only proof that the default report is unchanged, so it must be taken before T003.\n\n| Row | Arguments | Expected level |\n|-----|-----------|----------------|\n| M01 | `--loc 50 --files 2` | 0 (Quick) |\n| M02 | `--loc 200 --files 5 --api` | 1 (Baseline) |\n| M03 | `--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural` | 3 (Full) |\n| M04 | `--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --recommend-phases` | 3 (Full) |\n| M05 | `--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --no-recommend-phases` | 3 (Full) |\n| M06 | `--loc 100 --files 3 --json` | 0 (Quick) |\n| M07 | `--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --json --no-recommend-phases` | 3 (Full) |\n| M08 | `--help` | help text |\n| M09 | `--loc` | exit 1, `--loc requires a numeric value` |\n| M10 | `--loc 0 --files 0` | exit 1, `At least --loc or --files must be provided` |\n| M11 | `--bogus` | exit 1, `Unknown option: --bogus` |\n| M12 | `--phase-threshold 30 --loc 900 --files 20 --architectural --auth --api` | 3 (Full) |\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nPACKET=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\nmkdir -p \"$PACKET/scratch/golden\"\ni=0\nwhile IFS= read -r args; do\n  i=$((i + 1))\n  row=$(printf 'M%02d' \"$i\")\n  bash \"$SCRIPT\" $args > \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/$row.out\" 2> \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/$row.err\"\n  echo $? > \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/$row.code\"\ndone <<'ROWS'\n--loc 50 --files 2\n--loc 200 --files 5 --api\n--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural\n--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --recommend-phases\n--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --no-recommend-phases\n--loc 100 --files 3 --json\n--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --json --no-recommend-phases\n--help\n--loc\n--loc 0 --files 0\n--bogus\n--phase-threshold 30 --loc 900 --files 20 --architectural --auth --api\nROWS\nls \"$PACKET/scratch/golden\" | wc -l\ncat \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/M01.out\" | head -2\ncat \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/M09.code\" \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/M10.code\" \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/M11.code\"\n```\n\nExpected: `36` files; M01's second line is `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)`; each of the three `.code` files reads `1`, printed as three separate lines. If the loop stops early because `set -e` is active in the calling shell, run it with `set +e` first - the three error rows are expected to exit `1` and must still be recorded.\n\nRollback: `rm -r \"$PACKET/scratch/golden\"`.\n\nStop and escalate if: any row's level differs from the table, or a `.code` file is empty.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T003 Add the `QUIET_OUTPUT` global (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n\nFile: `$SCRIPT`. Anchor: the line `JSON_OUTPUT=false`, which T001 recorded at line 122.\n\nChange: add `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` on the line directly below `JSON_OUTPUT=false`, inside the same output-mode group and above the phase-recommendation flags. No comment line is added; the neighbouring globals carry none either.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\ngrep -n -A1 '^JSON_OUTPUT=false$' \"$SCRIPT\"\nbash -n \"$SCRIPT\" && echo SYNTAX_OK\n```\n\nExpected: `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` is the next line after `JSON_OUTPUT=false`; `SYNTAX_OK`.\n\nRollback: delete the `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` line.\n\nStop and escalate if: `JSON_OUTPUT=false` is not unique in the file, or `bash -n` fails.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T004 Add the `--quiet` parse arm (`$SCRIPT`)\n\nFile: `$SCRIPT`. Anchor: the text `    --json|-j)`, which T001 recorded at line 706.\n\nChange: insert one arm directly above the `--json|-j` arm:\n\n```bash\n    --quiet)\n      QUIET_OUTPUT=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n```\n\nThe arm takes no value, so it has no numeric guard. It sits above `--json|-j` rather than below it so the two output-mode switches stay adjacent and the `--json|-j` anchor does not move for T005.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\ngrep -n -B1 -A3 '^    --quiet)$' \"$SCRIPT\"\nbash -n \"$SCRIPT\" && echo SYNTAX_OK\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet | cat -A | head -3\n```\n\nExpected: the arm prints with its three body lines; `SYNTAX_OK`; the run prints the full report unchanged, because T005 has not added the guard yet - that is the expected intermediate state, and it confirms the flag parses without altering behaviour.\n\nRollback: delete the four inserted lines.\n\nStop and escalate if: `bash -n` fails, or the run reports `Unknown option: --quiet`.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T005 Add the quiet guard to `output_text()` (`$SCRIPT`)\n\nFile: `$SCRIPT`. Anchor: the text `output_text() {`, which T001 recorded at line 508, and the `echo \"\"` that follows it.\n\nChange: make the guard the first statement of the function body, above the leading `echo \"\"`:\n\n```bash\n  if [[ \"$QUIET_OUTPUT\" = true ]]; then\n    echo \"Recommended Level: ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL} (${LEVEL_NAME})\"\n    return 0\n  fi\n```\n\nThe format string is copied from the report's own level line rather than rewritten, so the two cannot drift. `output_json()` is not touched.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\ngrep -n -A5 '^output_text() {$' \"$SCRIPT\"\nbash -n \"$SCRIPT\" && echo SYNTAX_OK\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet | wc -l\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet\n```\n\nExpected: the guard is the first statement; `SYNTAX_OK`; the line count is `1`; the line reads `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)`.\n\nRollback: delete the four inserted lines.\n\nStop and escalate if: the line count is not `1`, the line text differs, or the guard landed outside `output_text()`.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T006 Document the flag in the header comment block (`$SCRIPT`)\n\nFile: `$SCRIPT`. Anchor: the header lines `#   --json, -j           Output in JSON format` and `#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --json`.\n\nChange: add one `OPTIONS` line below the `--json, -j` line, in the same column layout:\n\n```\n#   --quiet              Print only the recommended-level line (text output)\n```\n\nand one example below the existing JSON example:\n\n```\n#   Recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --quiet\n```\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\ngrep -c '^#   --quiet ' \"$SCRIPT\"\ngrep -c '^#   Recommend-level.sh .*--quiet$' \"$SCRIPT\"\n```\n\nExpected: `1` and `1`.\n\nRollback: delete the two inserted comment lines.\n\nStop and escalate if: either count is `0` after the edit, or the inserted line breaks the column alignment of the neighbouring options.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T007 Document the flag in `show_help()` (`$SCRIPT`)\n\nFile: `$SCRIPT`. Anchor: the help lines `  --json, -j           Output in JSON format` and `  recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --json`.\n\nChange: add one `OPTIONS` row below the `--json, -j` row, in the same two-column layout:\n\n```\n  --quiet              Print only the recommended-level line (text output)\n```\n\nand one example below the JSON example:\n\n```\n  # Quiet output for scripting\n  recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --quiet\n```\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --help | grep -c -- '--quiet'\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --help | grep -c 'SpecKit Level Recommendation Algorithm'\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --help > /dev/null; echo $?\n```\n\nExpected: `2` for the first command, one `OPTIONS` row and one example; `1` for the second, proving `--quiet --help` still prints the full help; `0` for the exit status.\n\nRollback: delete the three inserted help lines.\n\nStop and escalate if: the help text no longer matches the header block's wording, or `--help` exits non-zero.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T008 Static checks and a first smoke run (`$SCRIPT`)\n\nFile: `$SCRIPT`. Anchor: none.\n\nChange: no edit. Run the syntax check, confirm the interpreter, and run the two headline invocations before starting the matrix.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nbash -n \"$SCRIPT\" && echo SYNTAX_OK\n/bin/bash --version | head -1\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 50 --files 2 | sed -n '2p'\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 50 --files 2 --quiet\ncommand -v shellcheck >/dev/null && shellcheck -S warning \"$SCRIPT\" && echo SHELLCHECK_OK || echo SHELLCHECK_UNAVAILABLE\n```\n\nExpected: `SYNTAX_OK`; a `GNU bash, version 3.2` or newer line; `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)` from the report's second line; the same text as the only quiet line; `SHELLCHECK_OK` or `SHELLCHECK_UNAVAILABLE`.\n\nRollback: none - this task writes nothing.\n\nStop and escalate if: `bash -n` fails, or the two level lines differ.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T009 Prove the default report is unchanged across the twelve-row matrix\n\nFile: `scratch/verify/M*.out` (new directory). Anchor: none.\n\nChange: no edit. Rerun every row from T002 against the modified script into `scratch/verify/` and diff each pair.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nPACKET=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\nmkdir -p \"$PACKET/scratch/verify\"\ni=0\nwhile IFS= read -r args; do\n  i=$((i + 1))\n  row=$(printf 'M%02d' \"$i\")\n  bash \"$SCRIPT\" $args > \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/$row.out\" 2> \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/$row.err\"\n  echo $? > \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/$row.code\"\ndone <<'ROWS'\n--loc 50 --files 2\n--loc 200 --files 5 --api\n--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural\n--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --recommend-phases\n--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --no-recommend-phases\n--loc 100 --files 3 --json\n--loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --json --no-recommend-phases\n--help\n--loc\n--loc 0 --files 0\n--bogus\n--phase-threshold 30 --loc 900 --files 20 --architectural --auth --api\nROWS\ndiff -r \"$PACKET/scratch/golden\" \"$PACKET/scratch/verify\" && echo GOLDEN_IDENTICAL\n```\n\nExpected: `GOLDEN_IDENTICAL`, and `diff` exits `0`. Any printed difference is a failure, not a tolerance.\n\nRollback: `rm -r \"$PACKET/scratch/verify\"`.\n\nStop and escalate if: `diff` reports a difference. Restore the script with `git checkout -- \"$SCRIPT\"` and record which row drifted before retrying.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T010 Verify the quiet contract on every quiet row\n\nFile: `scratch/verify/quiet.txt` (new file). Anchor: none.\n\nChange: no edit. Run the eight quiet rows, write their stdout and exit codes, and confirm each produces exactly one line with the expected text.\n\n| Row | Arguments | Expected stdout | Exit |\n|-----|-----------|-----------------|------|\n| Q01 | `--quiet --loc 50 --files 2` | `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)` | 0 |\n| Q02 | `--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet` | `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)` | 0 |\n| Q03 | `--quiet --quiet --loc 200 --files 5 --api` | `Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)` | 0 |\n| Q04 | `--json --quiet --loc 100 --files 3` | the unchanged JSON document from M06 | 0 |\n| Q05 | `--quiet --no-recommend-phases --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural` | `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)` | 0 |\n| Q06 | `--quiet --help` | the full help text from M08 | 0 |\n| Q07 | `--quiet --loc` | empty stdout; stderr names the missing value | 1 |\n| Q08 | `--quiet` | empty stdout; stderr asks for `--loc` or `--files` | 1 |\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nPACKET=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n{\n  bash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --loc 50 --files 2\n  bash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet\n  bash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --quiet --loc 200 --files 5 --api\n  bash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --no-recommend-phases --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural\n} > \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/quiet.txt\"\nwc -l < \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/quiet.txt\"\ncat \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/quiet.txt\"\nhead -c 1 \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/quiet.txt\"; echo\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --json --quiet --loc 100 --files 3 | diff - \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/M06.out\" && echo JSON_UNCHANGED\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --help | diff - \"$PACKET/scratch/golden/M08.out\" && echo HELP_UNCHANGED\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --loc > /dev/null 2> \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/Q07.err\"; echo \"Q07=$?\"\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet > /dev/null 2> \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/Q08.err\"; echo \"Q08=$?\"\ncat \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/Q07.err\" \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/Q08.err\"\n```\n\nExpected: `4` lines; the four lines read `0 (Quick)`, `3 (Full)`, `1 (Baseline)`, `3 (Full)` in that order; `head -c 1` prints `R`, proving there is no leading blank line; `JSON_UNCHANGED`; `HELP_UNCHANGED`; `Q07=1`; `Q08=1`; the two stderr files carry the existing messages.\n\nRollback: `rm -f \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/quiet.txt\" \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/Q07.err\" \"$PACKET/scratch/verify/Q08.err\"`.\n\nStop and escalate if: any quiet row prints more than one line, a level differs from the table, or either precedence diff reports a change.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T011 Verify the flag's placement independence and the rejection path\n\nFile: none. Anchor: none.\n\nChange: no edit. Prove that argument position does not matter and that `--quiet` takes no value.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nSCRIPT=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\na=$(bash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet --loc 200 --files 5 --api)\nb=$(bash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc 200 --files 5 --api --quiet)\nc=$(bash \"$SCRIPT\" --loc --quiet 200 --files 5 --api 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\")\nprintf '%s\\n%s\\n%s\\n' \"$a\" \"$b\" \"$c\"\n[ \"$a\" = \"$b\" ] && echo POSITION_INDEPENDENT\nbash \"$SCRIPT\" --quiet 5 --loc 50 --files 2 > /dev/null 2>&1; echo \"VALUE_REJECTED=$?\"\n```\n\nExpected: `a` and `b` are both `Recommended Level: 1 (Baseline)`; `POSITION_INDEPENDENT`; `c` shows the existing numeric-value error and `exit=1`; `VALUE_REJECTED=1`.\n\nRollback: none - this task writes nothing.\n\nStop and escalate if: `a` and `b` differ, or the value-rejection path returns `0`.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] T012 Record the evidence and clean the scratch directory\n\nFile: `tasks.md` (this document) and `scratch/`. Anchor: none.\n\nChange: no code edit. Update the Verification Summary's `Verified` column for each item as its proof lands, mark every completed item `[x]` with its command and observed result, and remove the working files the packet does not need to keep. The two golden directories are evidence, so keep `scratch/golden/` and `scratch/verify/` until the packet closes; delete `scratch/anchors.md` once the anchors are no longer needed.\n\nCheck:\n\n```bash\nPACKET=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/check-completion.sh \"$PACKET\" || true\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$PACKET\" --strict | tail -3\n```\n\nExpected: `check-completion.sh` reports the checklist state without a P0 or P1 item marked complete and unevidenced; `validate.sh` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n\nRollback: none - the evidence is additive.\n\nStop and escalate if: a completed P0 or P1 item has no evidence line, or `validate.sh` prints a failure.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] Code passes lint/format checks\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No console errors or warnings\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling implemented\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] Code follows project patterns\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Manual testing complete\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed, or instance-only status proven by grep.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for changed helpers, policies, schema fields, response fields, docs, and tests.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Security/path/parser/redaction fixes include adversarial table tests for delimiter, joined-input, outside-root, no-op, and fallback cases.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile env/global-state variant executed when tests or code read process-wide state.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a fix SHA or explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation implemented\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] Auth/authz working correctly\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Code comments adequate\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README updated (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files in scratch/ only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] scratch/ cleaned before completion\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 15 | 0/15 |\n| P1 Items | 23 | 0/23 |\n| P2 Items | 9 | 0/9 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-26\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] Architecture decisions documented in decision-record.md\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] All ADRs have status (Proposed/Accepted)\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path documented (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] Response time targets met (NFR-P01)\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] Throughput targets met (NFR-P02)\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] Load testing completed\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] Performance benchmarks documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented and tested\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] Feature flag configured (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] Monitoring/alerting configured\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] Runbook created\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Deployment runbook reviewed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review completed\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses compatible\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP Top 10 checklist completed\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling compliant with requirements\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation complete (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| Packet author | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| Operator | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| Packet author | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n---\n\n## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n- [ ] Read this document and confirm the task id, its file, its quoted anchor and its line number.\n- [ ] Re-read the file the task edits; confirm the quoted anchor still sits where T001 recorded it and belongs to the function the task names.\n- [ ] Confirm the task is not `[B]`; if it is, record the blocker and stop before editing.\n- [ ] Confirm T002's golden capture exists and is non-empty before any edit to `$SCRIPT`. Without it, the unchanged-output claim cannot be proven.\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Run T001 to T012 in order. T002 is `[P]` only against T001, because the capture must exist before T003 edits the script. |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Write only `$SCRIPT` and `$PACKET/scratch/`. Every other path is read-only. |\n| TASK-PROOF | Run the task's check and read both its output and its exit status before marking the task `[x]`. |\n| TASK-ANCHOR | Locate the quoted text. A moved line is not a changed edit; an absent anchor is a stop, not a nearby edit. |\n| TASK-COMMENT | No comment, help row or example added by this packet carries a task id, an AC-id or a packet number. |\n| TASK-OUTPUT | Never \"fix\" a golden-diff difference by recapturing the baseline. The baseline is the pre-change contract; a difference means the edit is wrong. |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\nAfter each task: `Task T### complete. Files: <paths>. Proof: <command> -> <observed output/exit>.` At a phase boundary, report the task range, the files changed and the gate that passed.\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\nIf a task cannot run, stop and record the blocker in `scratch/blocked.md` with the task id, the command that failed and its output. Do not substitute a different file, a different value or a different command. A `[B]` task stays blocked until its dependency's proof exists; a failed gate is repaired, not waived.\n\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":0,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":2}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
